# Trivy CVE ignore list for Alpine base image (mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/aspnet:10.0-alpine)
# These are OS-level vulnerabilities with no upstream fix or not exploitable in FunkArr.

# glibc: heap buffer overflow via attacker-controlled fopen mode string
# Not exploitable: FunkArr does not pass user-controlled strings to fopen
CVE-2025-4802

# openssl: invalid pointer dereference in CMP server via crafted protectionAlg
# Not exploitable: FunkArr does not use CMP (Certificate Management Protocol)
CVE-2025-3416

# openssl: heap buffer overflow in CMS key unwrapping
# Not exploitable: FunkArr does not use CMS key unwrapping
CVE-2025-4575

# openssl: ChaCha20-Poly1305 and AES-OCB decryption with empty associated data
# Low severity, requires specific cipher usage patterns not present in FunkArr
CVE-2025-3765

# openssl: CMP indefinite cache growth of ExtraCerts
# Not exploitable: FunkArr does not use CMP
CVE-2025-3784

# openssl: excessive memory use buffering DTLS records for a future epoch
# Not exploitable: FunkArr does not use DTLS
CVE-2025-3786

# icu: stack buffer overflow in SRBRoot::addTag function (genrb binary)
# Not exploitable: only triggered via genrb binary, not at runtime
CVE-2025-5222
